"}]}

{"id": "fabc538d-737d-4899-843a-60753505a2eb", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "I'll break down your Bedrock costs by model and usage type, comparing October with September and November to date. Then I'll look at where you can cut spend.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_jPAUQvScISOujlPGzC3re1", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "bedrock-cost-breakdown", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["verifying-with-docs"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Identify which Amazon Bedrock model(s) drove the spend increase last month and recommend concrete ways to cut cost.",
  "context": "The user says their Amazon Bedrock bill roughly doubled last month. Today is 2026-11-24, so 'last month' = October 2026; compare against September 2026 and also show November 2026 month-to-date. Use read-only AWS Cost Explorer calls (us-east-1 endpoint). Start with the agent space account 012345678901_1, and use list_associations to check whether other associated AWS accounts also have Bedrock spend (check each with read-only calls; for a payer/management account use LINKED_ACCOUNT grouping). Do NOT make any mutating calls.",
  "resources": ["AWS account 012345678901_1", "Service: Amazon Bedrock (also check 'Claude (Amazon Bedrock Edition)' and other third-party model SERVICE names sold via Bedrock/Marketplace, since Anthropic/Meta/Mistral/Cohere etc. models may bill under their own service names)"],
  "timeframe": "2026-09-01T00:00:00Z to 2026-11-24T00:00:00Z, monthly granularity (and daily for October if a spike date needs pinning down)",
  "criteria": "1) Total Bedrock cost per month Sep/Oct/Nov-MTD with delta. 2) Breakdown by model (derive from USAGE_TYPE, e.g. model name + input-tokens/output-tokens/provisioned throughput/batch/custom-model/knowledge-base/guardrail/agent line items) and by region and by account. Identify which model/usage types account for most of the increase, and whether it is a volume (tokens) increase, a new model adoption, provisioned throughput/model units, or a shift to a pricier model. If a spike is concentrated on specific days, say which. 3) If cheaply possible, correlate with caller/application (e.g. CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock metrics InputTokenCount/OutputTokenCount/Invocations by ModelId, and whether model invocation logging exists) to say who/what is calling the top model. 4) Cost-cutting recommendations tied to the findings (e.g. cheaper model tier, prompt caching, batch inference, provisioned throughput right-sizing, token limits, knowledge base/vector store costs, guardrails, intelligent prompt routing) — verify any pricing/feature claims via documentation lookup. Return a concise report with numbers in USD, a ranked table of top cost drivers, the key findings, and any data you could not access (e.g. missing ce:GetCostAndUsage permission)."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Analyze Bedrock cost by model with Cost Explorer"}], "created_at": null}

{"id": "e9fa2239-49df-4f7f-9d15-609c7e6ac68e", "role": "assistant", "block_type": "thinking", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "September shows no data at all in this account, which means the "doubled" claim doesn't hold up here—maybe the spending happened in a different account or the account itself wasn't created until October. I'm now summing October's costs by service, tallying Opus 4 totals across several line items to get 28.62, and starting on the Sonnet figures next.

